StepsStep 1: Download node.js from https://nodejs.org
Step 2: Install node.js by following the installation. After installation 
complete, install Visual Studio Code (VS Code).
Step 3: Open VS Code and create a new project folder.
Step 4: Click File → Open Folder, create a new folder named My-First-app. Open 
it in VS Code.
Step 5: Open the terminal in VS Code by selecting Terminal → New Terminal.
Step 6: In the terminal, type the following command:
npm create vite@latest
If it shows an error named PowerShell block script execution, then put the 
command:
Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope CurrentUser RemoteSigned
Step 7: When prompted, enter the project name:
Project Name: my-react-app
Step 8: Select the react framework using the arrow keys and press Enter. Then 
select javascript as the variant.
Step 9: Navigate the project folder and install the required packages:
cd my-react-app
npm install
Step 10: Start the development server by running:
npm run dev
Step 11: The Vite development server will start and display a local URL:
http://localhost:5173/
Step 12: Copy the URL and paste it in your web browser. The default React 
application page will be displayed.
